====Noun====
[[File:Boxers Brief 1.jpg|thumb|'''Pants''' (United Kingdom)]]
{{en-plural noun|attr=pant}}

# {{senseid|en|outer garment}} {{lb|en|chiefly|North America|Australia|New Zealand|South Africa|India|Philippines|Singapore|Northern England}} An outer [[garment]] that covers the body from the [[waist]] downwards, covering each leg separately, usually as far as the [[ankle]]s; [[trousers]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1933|author=w:Kenneth Roberts|title=Rabble in Arms|pageurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20121208060213/http://books.google.com.au/books?id=IgSmHZP4O14C&pg=PA220&dq=pants|page=220|year_published=1996
|passage=“But they cover the legs,” Joseph explained. “That is the only reason my people wear '''pants''': to cover the legs in the winter, or when traveling through rough country, full of thorns. In warm weather, or in open country, '''pants''' are unnecessary, uncomfortable, and foolish.”}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=1970-06|author=traditional|artist=w:Steeleye Span|album=Hark! The Village Wait|track=4|title=The Blackleg Miner|url=https://genius.com/Steeleye-span-blackleg-miner-lyrics|passage=It's in the evening after dark when the blackleg miner creeps to work. With his moleskin '''pants''' and his dirty shirt, there goes the blackleg miner.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989|author=w:Bryce Courtenay|title=w:The Power of One|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=c1B4atNBSWwC&pg=PA427&dq=pants|page=427|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2006
|passage=Then he gave me a last desperate push and I tripped over the shorts caught around my ankles and fell down. I tried to pull my '''pants''' up with my boxing gloves but without success.{{...}}In those days nobody wore underpants and I was bare-arsed and fancy free in front of everyone.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|editor=Ronald C. Eng|title=Mountaineering: The Freedom of the Hills|edition=8th|publisher=The Mountaineers Books|location=US|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=QupdBAEgpGEC&pg=PA24&dq=pants|page=24
|passage=Look for '''pants''' with reinforced seats and knees and full-length side zippers that make it possible to put the '''pants''' on while you are wearing boots, crampons, skis, or snowshoes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=w:Octavia E. Butler|title=[[w:Fledgling (novel)|Fledgling]]|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=OiJI19ot4BsC&pg=PA12&dq=pants|page=12
|passage=I rolled up the legs of the '''pants''', then I went back into the trees.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 27, 2012
|author=Nathan Rabin
|title=TV: Review: THE SIMPSONS (CLASSIC): “New Kid On The Block” (season 4, episode 8; originally aired 11/12/1992)
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/new-kid-on-the-block,75341/
|page=
|passage=The episode also opens with an inspired bit of business for Homer, who blithely refuses to acquiesce to an elderly neighbor’s utterly reasonable request that he help make the process of selling her house easier by wearing '''pants''' when he gallivants about in front of windows, throw out his impressive collection of rotting Jack-O-Lanterns from previous Halloweens and take out his garbage, as it’s attracting wildlife (cue moose and Northern Exposure theme song).}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2014-01-13
|title=Blackburn man hid machete down his trousers
|journal=The Lancashire Telegraph
|url=https://www.lancashiretelegraph.co.uk/news/10932221.blackburn-man-hid-machete-trousers/
|passage=Taylor was seen nearby and had a three foot machete down his '''pants'''.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK}} An [[undergarment]] that covers the [[genitals]] and often the [[buttocks]] and the neighbouring parts of the body; [[underpants]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1939|author=w:Raymond Chandler|title=The Big Sleep|page=39|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2011
|passage=I decided to pass up her underclothes, not from feelings of delicacy, but because I couldn't see myself putting her '''pants''' on and snapping her brassière.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1976|author=w:Nathan H. Azrin; Richard M. Foxx|title=Toilet Training in Less Than a Day|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=DPOXKXBr-TkC&q=pants|page=127|year_published=1988
|passage=Big girls get candy for dry '''pants'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1984|author=w:Martin Amis|title=Money|page=183|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2005
|passage=As she bent over the intercom the little skirt went peek-a-boo and you could see white '''pants''' cupping her buttocks like a bra.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang}} [[rubbish|Rubbish]]; something [[worthless]].
#: ''You're talking '''pants'''!''
#: ''The film was a load [or pile] of '''pants'''.''

